title: 'people-westend, yet-another-parachain: add the missing parachain-system storage migrations'

doc:
  - audience: [Runtime Dev, Node Operator]
    description: |
      `cumulus-pallet-parachain-system` is at storage version 4 (`LastProcessedHrmpMessage`
      became `InboundHrmpMessageId` in #12876), but the People Westend and Yet Another
      Parachain runtimes never listed `migration::v3::Migration` and
      `migration::MigrateV3ToV4`, unlike the other Westend system chains. They now run both as
      permanent migrations. Without them, the first runtime upgrade of such a chain leaves the
      pallet at its old storage version with a value the new code cannot decode: every block
      that processes inbound HRMP messages logs `Corrupted state` until the value is rewritten,
      and `try-runtime` rejects the upgrade on the storage-version mismatch. Both migrations
      are no-ops once the on-chain version is current.

crates:
  - name: people-westend-runtime
    bump: minor
  - name: yet-another-parachain-runtime
    bump: minor
